==Strategy==
There are two ways to tackle this stage. The least recommended one, but most accessible, involves the use of a large amount of meatshields and ranged attackers, such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], allowing you to pick off the support while holding the line and slowly killing the main threat.

If you can, however, you should rush the stage. Awakened Bahamut is the prime choice here, preferably with fast meatshields like [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]] or, if on 4-crown difficulty, [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]]. Bahamut should be able to finish the stage without further trouble. He will struggle a little in 4-crown unless he is backed by Attack Combos or has his explosion talent unlocked (damage on his first hit untalented is 97500 at level 40, while the minimum amount of damage needed to knockback Alois in 4-crown is 105,000), but even one Attack Up (Sm) Combo or an unlocked explosion talent is enough to give him the necessary damage so that meatshields can catch up. The remaining slots could be saved for worker combos.

